<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR falls as peso rates soften.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR falls as peso rates soften.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) dropped across all maturities on Thursday following the weakness in the overnight rates, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The PHIBOR are just reflecting the movement in the spot rates of the peso,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Overnight rates dropped to 12.59375 percent from the previous 12.78125.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>		    Sept 5		   Sept 4</p>
<p> 1 W		12 15/16		13 1/4</p>
<p> 2 W		12  3/4		 13 1/16</p>
<p> 1 M		12  3/8		 12 9/16</p>
<p> 2 M		11 15/16		12 1/8</p>
<p> 3 M		11  7/8		 11 15/16</p>
<p> 6 M		11 13/16		11 7/8</p>
<p> 12M		12			12 1/16</p>
<p> VAL		6-Sep		   5-Sep</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418936 Fax 8176267</p>
